  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "What number is one third of the way from \\(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\) to \\(\\dfrac{3}{4}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{12}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{12}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "One third of the way from \\(\\frac14\\) to \\(\\frac34\\) means starting at \\(\\frac14\\) and adding one third of the distance between the endpoints. That distance is\n\\[\n\\frac34-\\frac14=\\frac12,\n\\]\nso the amount to add is \\(\\frac13\\cdot\\frac12=\\frac16\\). The requested number is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac14+\\frac16\n=\\frac3{12}+\\frac2{12}\n=\\frac5{12}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\frac5{12}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
